Homepage: https://github.com/FreeMixer/omx-clap-core
Description: use CLAP and LV2 plugins on a JACK rig, driven like mod-host
 omx-clap-host hosts CLAP and LV2 plugins in a live JACK or PipeWire rig.
 Each plugin runs as a JACK client with its own ports, and an instrument
 gets a MIDI input as well. Anything that already controls mod-host can
 control it over the same socket with the same commands. An LV2 plugin,
 added by its URI, runs natively: a real LV2 instance loaded through lilv,
 with no emulation and no wrapper process. The LV2 adapter linked into the
 host maps the host interface, presenting the plugin's ports and controls
 as CLAP ports and parameters, and loads lilv when the first one is added.
 .
 It comes with omx-clap-scan, which lists what is in a CLAP bundle and
 survives a plugin that crashes while loading.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

